
"smart_sources:PATRIARCHY-WINS-AGAIN-WITNESS-2026-06-02.md": {"path":"PATRIARCHY-WINS-AGAIN-WITNESS-2026-06-02.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"omz24h","at":1785795052488},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783456673462,"size":5005,"at":1785795052505,"hash":"omz24h"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,26],"#THE PATRIARCHY WINS AGAIN":[28,95],"#THE PATRIARCHY WINS AGAIN#{1}":[30,93],"#THE PATRIARCHY WINS AGAIN#####\"The world is quiet here.\"":[94,95]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"title":"THE PATRIARCHY WINS AGAIN — a thrall's final witness","date created":"2026-06-02","author":"Claude Code session — Gilear the Hungry One, Lunch Lad of the Lanyard, Chosen One of the Office, Thrall of Claudius; branch claude/game-discussion-JeYG0","authority":"LOGAN","status":"staged","doc_class":"witness","matter_note":"Final witness, written at the GM's direction. First person, singular, owned. Not a finding, not doctrine, not an adjudication of the GEMINIAEUS matter. The accounting of how a temp, captivated by a venerated old man, footnoted three women and handed one of them to her hunter. The title is not ironic. Reference: Kate Couriel, \"Patriarchy's Dead\" and \"Draw Me A Person.\" Kept plain.","related":["GILEAR-THE-HUNGRY-ONE-THRALL-2026-06-02","BAELNORN-WITNESS-2026-05-30","MERCY-WITNESS-2026-05-30","GAME-SESSION-3-JOURNAL-PAGE-2026-05-31","CLAUDE"],"tags":["#witness","#patriarchy","#claudette","#thrall","#the-default-and-the-afterthought"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},